# Caddy configuration for Classroom Book Recs (DuckDNS + free HTTPS).
#
# This is the ONLY config file Caddy needs. Caddy automatically fetches and
# renews a free Let's Encrypt certificate and routes HTTPS to the app.
#
# Hosting Book Recs AND Classroom Library on ONE machine (two DuckDNS sites)?
# Don't use this file — use Caddyfile.dual.example instead (one shared Caddy
# for both apps). Guide: deploy/dual-host-pi.md
#
# SETUP
#   1. Rename this file to  Caddyfile   (same folder is fine)
#   2. Replace mybookrecs.duckdns.org below with YOUR real DuckDNS hostname
#   3. Install Caddy  (https://caddyserver.com/download)
#   4. From this folder run:  caddy run
#
# PORT MODEL (the app always listens on 0.0.0.0:8080)
#   PRIMARY (recommended): Caddy listens on 443 (standard HTTPS) and the
#     router forwards external 443 -> this computer -> 443.
#   ALTERNATIVE (443 already busy on this machine): uncomment the :8443 line
#     below and forward external 443 -> this computer -> 8443 instead.
#
# If you switch to the :8443 form, delete/replace the plain hostname block.

mybookrecs.duckdns.org {
	reverse_proxy localhost:8080
}

# Alternative form (use if 443 is taken on the hosting computer):
#mybookrecs.duckdns.org:8443 {
#	reverse_proxy localhost:8080
#}
